# Generate as many dungeon levels as one session can, and pass turns on each one.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/dive.keys 1
#
# Where explore.keys stays on one level and fills logs/errors.log with what
# happens during play, this fills it with what happens during MAP GENERATION.
# That is a different body of code and a different set of defects -- the first
# one found, inc-upw.3, fires inside Map::Generate and only once per game,
# so an ordinary session gives it a single chance to appear.
#
# Wizard mode's 'Ascend / Descend Depth' is what makes this possible: it
# generates a level on demand instead of waiting for the player to find the
# stairs. Entering wizard mode needs a confirmation the first time and not
# afterwards, which is why the first line differs from the rest.
#
# THE DEPTH CEILING. This file asks for 14 depth jumps -- 2 down to 10, then
# back up to 2 -- and none is above DUN_DEPTH 10 (lib/dungeon.irh:17). Wizard
# 'Ascend / Descend Depth' rejects any depth above DUN_DEPTH
# (src/Debug.cpp:805-809). The 22 refused jumps above 10 were removed under
# inc-wrc40: their waits and searches all ran on the depth 10 level (seed 1 on
# the inc-y2fkq build: 250755 turns and 347 s before, 14675 turns and 22 s
# after). No key script may ask for a depth above 10.
#
# THE WAITS. Between jumps the character waits ('.') instead of walking. The
# walk keys used to lead into whatever terrain the seed put in their path, and
# a step into warning terrain asks "Confirm enter the ...?" (src/Move.cpp),
# which this script never answered, so the session stalled and the gate counted
# it as NO GAMEPLAY. Waiting passes the same number of turns, so monsters still
# move and their AI still runs, and no movement prompt can appear. Each wait
# count equals the number of movement keys it replaced. inc-nx0z.
#
# THE DEATH PROMPT. The gate settings turn on OPT_NODEATH, so a death asks
# "You die... Die? [yn]" (src/Fight.cpp). Unanswered, it swallowed every later
# key, and no session played its whole script. The @while line before each
# jump answers n, so the character cheats death and the dive goes on; it sends
# nothing when no death prompt is on screen. inc-nx0z.
#
# THE LAST BOX. The last jump can land in a room that opens a description box
# ("#------" border). The line before the final dump closes any such box, so
# the final screen shows the map on every seed; it sends nothing when no box is
# open and spends no game turn. inc-nx0z.
#
# Generated the same way as explore.keys, seeded 20260816.

@include chargen.keys

@dump:arrival

@while "You die... Die?" n
w y p "2" ENTER
.*19 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "3" ENTER
.*17 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "4" ENTER
.*13 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "5" ENTER
.*24 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "6" ENTER
@dump:depth6
.*17 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "7" ENTER
.*17 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "8" ENTER
.*13 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "9" ENTER
.*17 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "10" ENTER
.*17 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "10" ENTER
.*22 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "8" ENTER
.*15 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "6" ENTER
@dump:depth6
.*19 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "4" ENTER
.*19 s .*2
@while "You die... Die?" n
w p "2" ENTER

@while "#------" SPACE
@dump:final
@quit
